  "summary_md": "Softlines and electrical equipment reports highlight a consumer-spending fork—value-oriented off-price remains robust (CTRN posted accelerating comps on strong Black-family demand), while inflation continues to squeeze budget-focused mall retailers (CATO, ZUMZ reversed to negative in May). The most eye-catching repositioning is the rush into AI data-center power: FCEL’s pipeline exploded on clean baseload demand and PPSI’s off-grid PRYMUS platform won a logistics award, while BIRD’s controversial pivot from footwear to AI infrastructure—complete with an AWS-veteran CEO and GPU financing—keeps debate alive. Elsewhere, liquidity and conversion risks recur among early-stage battery/energy names (SDST, STI, DFLI), tempering thematic enthusiasm.",
